@subheading Procedures

@c Note: in this section, the @var{typelib} argument is [must be] a
@c pointer to a @code{GITypelib}.


@anchor{gi-type-tag-get-ffi-type}
@deffn Procedure gi-type-tag-get-ffi-type type-tag is-pointer?

Returns a (pointer to) @code{ffi-type} corresponding to the platform
default C ABI for @var{type-tag} and @var{is-pointer?}.

The @var{info} argument is (must be) a valid @ref{%gi-type-tag},
otherwise an exception is raised.

The @var{is-pointer?} argument, @code{#t} or @code{#f}, to indicate
whether or not this is a pointer type.
@end deffn


@anchor{g-type-info-get-ffi-type}
@deffn Procedure g-type-info-get-ffi-type info

Returns an (pointer to) @code{ffi-type} corresponding to the platform
default C ABI for @var{info}.

The @var{info} argument is [must be] a pointer to a @code{GITypeInfo}.
@end deffn


@anchor{gi-type-info-extract-ffi-return-value}
@deffn Procedure gi-type-info-extract-ffi-return-value type-info @
       ffi-value gi-argument

Returns nothing.

Extract the correct bits from @var{ffi-value} into @var{gi-argument}.

The @var{type-info} argument is the GITypeInfo of @var{ffi-value}. The
@var{ffi-value} argument is a pointer to a GIFFIReturnValue union
containing the value from the @code{ffi_call()}. The @var{gi-argument}
argument is a pointer to an allocated GIArgument.
@end deffn


@anchor{g-callable-info-prepare-closure}
@deffn Procedure g-callable-info-prepare-closure info @
                 ffi-cif ffi-closure-callback user-data

Returns the native address of the closure or @code{#f} on error.

@example
The procedure has been deprecated since version @code{1.72} and should
not be used in newly-written code. Use
@ref{g-callable-info-create-closure} instead.
@end example

The return value should be freed by calling
@code{g-callable-info-free-closure}.
@end deffn
